# Project: Handmade Diya E-commerce Website – End-to-End DevOps Implementation

## Project Objective

I want to build a real-world e-commerce website to sell my handmade diyas.

My objective is not only to develop a website but also to implement a complete DevOps lifecycle, starting from application development and ending with a production deployment accessible to real users through my purchased domain.

Act as my Senior Full Stack Developer, DevOps Engineer, Kubernetes Engineer and AWS Architect.

Guide me step by step throughout the project.

## Phase 1: Application Development (Frontend + Backend + Database)

First, develop a complete working e-commerce application based on the following requirements.

### Frontend Requirements
- Create an attractive, responsive e-commerce website.
- Display handmade diya products.
- Product listing page.
- Product details page.
- Product name, description, features and price.
- Product images and image gallery.
- Shopping cart.
- Customer-friendly user interface.
- Admin login page.
- Admin dashboard.

### Backend Requirements
- Develop backend REST APIs.
- Add new products.
- Update existing products.
- Delete products.
- Fetch all products.
- Fetch individual product details.
- Admin authentication and authorization.
- Product image upload.
- Order management APIs.

### Database Requirements
- Integrate a database with the backend.
- Store product information.
- Store product name, description, features and price.
- Store product image references.
- Store customer and order information.
- Implement proper database relationships.

### Suggested Technology Stack
- Frontend: React.js
- Backend: Node.js + Express.js
- Database: PostgreSQL
- ORM: Prisma

The complete application must work locally before proceeding to the next phase.

